      "name": "Request, Aggregate, Bypass: How Attackers Can Evade LLM Safety Classifiers",
      "description": "TL;DR; Our security assessment of LiteLLM (v1.77.7), a widely used open-source LLM gateway, uncovered multiple high-impact vulnerabilities (tracked as CVE-2026-35029, CVE-2026-59823) which have been resolved as of LiteLLM version 1.83.9. The most significant issues stemmed from a missing authorization check on the /config/update endpoint, which allowed any authenticated user (including low-privileged accounts) to modify the [\u2026] The post When LLM Gateways Go Wrong: Findings from LiteLLM appeared first on Check Point Research .",
